    "result_text": "The full suite is green \u2014 `AcceptanceTest` is the only test class (`AcceptanceBase` and `AuditLogCapture` are support classes). `BUILD SUCCESS`.\n\n## Summary\n\nAdded `checkDigit` = a single Luhn check digit computed over the digits of `customerCode`, following the codebase's established pattern for derived, never-persisted fields.\n\nThree changes, each in its proper home:\n\n1. **`util/LuhnCheckDigit.java`** (new) \u2014 a small single-responsibility utility with `LuhnCheckDigit.of(String)`, mirroring how `getLocality()` delegates to `CityLocality`. The algorithm matches the spec: right-to-left, doubling from the rightmost digit with nines cast out, non-digits skipped, result `(10 - sum%10) % 10`.\n\n2. **`model/Owner.java`** \u2014 a derived `getCheckDigit()` getter alongside the other derived getters (`getLocality`, `getMembershipLevel`, `getContactPreference`, `getIdentityKey`), delegating to the utility. No DB column, since it's derived.\n\n3. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 a `checkDigit` read-only integer (0\u20139) property on the Owner schema, next to `customerCode`.\n\nNo new wiring was needed: MapStruct's `OwnerMapper.toOwnerDto` maps `getCheckDigit()` to the generated `OwnerDto.checkDigit` by name, so every endpoint serializing an owner (POST/GET/PUT) now includes it automatically.",
